I've led at least half a dozen wizards, a barbarian and an
archeologist to the slaughter this morning, and the one currently
trying his luck is a dopppleganger wizard. He happened to start with a
ring of poly control (yay!) and a ring of protection from
shapechangers.

It seems to me dopplegangers should get some kind of negative effect
from the ring of protection from shapechangers. Maybe it just
shouldn't work, or they should be blasted by it's power or stunned for
a few rounds, or perhaps it should simply autocurse. Maybe
confusion+autocurse..?

A negative effect of some sort would go some way to offsetting the
huge potential bonus of shapechanger characters starting with a ring
of poly control- after all there is code in the game (I believe) to
prevent you starting with a ring/wand of poly + ring of poly control,
but nothing to prevent intrinsic poly+ ring of pc.

At the very least putting the ring on could show some sort of YAFM:
"You are protected from yourself." Or when you take it off "You feel
as though you are a hazard to yourself." Of course this would give
dopplegangers a further advantage since the message could be used to
ID the ring...

